1
00:00:03,634 --> 00:00:11,403
Units first: centimetres, on a twenty centimetre grid.

2
00:00:11,453 --> 00:00:17,433
Script objects are built by code,
so one design can take many sizes.

3
00:00:17,483 --> 00:00:26,813
Edit Script shows the code:
parameters first, then the geometry.

4
00:00:26,863 --> 00:00:36,563
$NUMBER adds a field to the panel.
$HOTSPOT adds a handle you can drag.

5
00:00:36,613 --> 00:00:40,085
Close the editor to get back to the model.

6
00:00:40,135 --> 00:00:45,956
To size it, press G for a grid
helper on the face of the bookcase.

7
00:00:46,006 --> 00:00:52,226
Now drag the hotspot along that grid.
The bookcase is rebuilt as it moves.

8
00:00:52,276 --> 00:00:59,378
Parameters sit in the Object Instance
panel. Set this one to 5 shelves.

9
00:00:59,428 --> 00:01:09,814
Awesome. Move Copy it: pick its corner,
then a grid point further along.

10
00:01:09,864 --> 00:01:19,436
Make the copy shorter, on that same
grid helper. The first stays as it was.

11
00:01:19,486 --> 00:01:22,586
Clear Guides to tidy up.

12
00:01:22,636 --> 00:01:32,651
Wooow! One script, two independent
bookcases, both still adjustable.
